% ---------------------------------------------------------------------

% READ-STATE: FULL TEXT (queried), arXiv HTML of v3.
% CONFIRMED TWICE, independently:
%   (1) arXiv abstract page, arxiv.org/abs/2606.00419
%   (2) arXiv full-text HTML, arxiv.org/html/2606.00419v3
%
% PREPRINT ONLY. Checked for a peer-reviewed venue: the arXiv record carries NO
% journal-ref and NO comments field naming a venue. Four versions: v1
% 2026-05-29, v2 2026-06-02, v3 2026-06-08, v4 2026-07-07. Cite as a preprint
% and say so in the prose, as this document already does for Chronos-2 and
% TabPFN-TS.
%
% WHAT IT CLAIMS, quoted: "We introduce the first parameter-free algorithm for
% group-conditional online conformal prediction, that we dub Portfolios for
% Online Group Conformal (POGO)." Note the claim is to be first at being
% PARAMETER-FREE, not at anything about group construction.
%
% RELEVANCE TO C7, AND THE LIMIT OF IT. Groups enter as given objects: a
% "collection of soft indicator functions" where each "represents the
% likelihood of input X belonging to group j". The paper does not discuss group
% misspecification, within-group heterogeneity or zero-inflation. Its stock
% experiment DOES define groups by day-of-week calendar markers, so
% calendar-defined Mondrian groups are NOT novel; what is unaddressed is a
% partition that is correct about availability and wrong about the score
% distribution.
%
% REGIME. MIMIC-IV, ~26,000 test samples, groups by race/insurance/sex; stocks
% (AAPL, DAL, BA) ~2,500 trading days each. Ellel's 66 traded days sit outside
% this by roughly an order of magnitude. Code: github.com/beepulbharti/pogo
% (not inspected; licence unverified).
